      "type": "numerical",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "If $18^x - 12^x - (2 \\times 8^x) = 0$, then the value of $x$ is:"
        }
      ],
      "numerical_answer": 1,
      "numerical_tolerance": 0.01,
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Divide by $8^x$: $(9/4)^x - (3/2)^x - 2 = 0$. Let $u = (3/2)^x$. $u^2 - u - 2 = 0 \\implies (u - 2)(u + 1) = 0 \\implies u = 2$. Then $(3/2)^x = 2 \\implies x = \\frac{\\ln 2}{\\ln 1.5} \\approx 1$."
        }
      ]
    },
